From e903693765c24443e0f78498736c7f1a4892b8b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:01:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 82/98] pco, pvr: copy uniform buffer ranges into shared
 registers

Every uniform buffer load was a memory load in each shader invocation,
so a vertex shader reading three matrices issued about a dozen loads per
vertex. zink puts all GL uniforms in a uniform buffer, and replacing two
of the matrices of glmark2's phong vertex shader by constants alone made
the scene 33% faster.

pco now picks, per uniform buffer, the dword range read at constant
offsets (at most 64 dwords per buffer, 128 and 4 buffers per shader) and
reads it from shared registers. The descriptor upload program copies the
range from the buffer at each draw: the driver looks up the buffer in
the bound descriptor set when it fills in the program's data, and points
the copy at the zero page if the descriptor is null or smaller than the
range (a bounds checked shader then takes the path that doesn't read the
copy). Bounds checked loads have computed offsets, so they keep reading
memory. Bindings that may change after bind or be partially bound are
left alone, since their descriptors can't be read when the draw is
recorded.

glmark2-es2 through zink, off-screen 800x600, FPS of two runs each,
before -> after: build 498/490 -> 730/751, phong 238/237 -> 425/423,
gouraud 368/367 -> 668/656, bump high-poly 145/144 -> 287/290, terrain
12/12 -> 18/19, jellyfish 148/144 -> 171/171, the others unchanged.

CTS: new uniform buffer sample (4773: ubo, binding_model uniform buffer
and dynamic offset cases), robustness list (4025), 5062 list,
loops/indexing/graphicsfuzz list (6428), compute.pipeline (1235),
dynamic_rendering sample (6745), TFBC list (9170), synchronization
(1718): identical to before. glmark2 --validate: 27 pass, 0 fail.
